{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Ibn Majah","section":{"32":{"eng-name":"Chapters on Dress","ara-name":"كتاب اللباس"}},"section_detail":{"32":{"hadithnumber_first":3550,"hadithnumber_last":3656,"arabicnumber_first":3550,"arabicnumber_last":3656}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3617,"arabicnumber":3617,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Huraira : Le Messager d’Allah ﷺ a dit : “Aucun de vous ne doit marcher avec une seule sandale ou un seul chausson en cuir. Qu’il les enlève toutes les deux ou qu’il marche avec les deux.”","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}],"reference":{"book":32,"hadith":68},"chapter":{"id":29,"ara-name":"باب الْمَشْىِ فِي النَّعْلِ الْوَاحِدِ","eng-name":"Walking in one sandal","isFirstHadith":true}}]}